// TEST: a block lambda applied to a kernel cell over a generic array, instantiated at Bool (rejects)
// ============================================================================
// R10 remainder: the kernel cell `v` is `outer`'s generic element, so the link
// between it and `f`'s open parameter is never decided inside the declaration;
// at the declaration's end the arithmetic `f`'s body deferred on its parameter
// (`x + x`) moves to that generic variable and is judged per instance --
// `outer([true, false])` is refused, spanned (functions/895 is the scalar
// form). No numeric type is bound. The base printed `r = [true, false]`.
// ============================================================================
function outer(b) = {
    let f = lambda(x) -> x + x
    method_for(b) <@> lambda(v) -> f(v) |> compute
}
let r = outer([true, false])
// ERROR: BL3001 @ 13:15
